 currently experienced  across the globe there's no silver  bullet here to solve this type of  inflation driven by global pressures and  supply chains  the best thing that canadians can do is  be patient as for what's in the update  major proposed spending measures are  already on the table 7.4 billion dollars  in retooled pandemic benefits were  announced in october bill c-2 was  introduced in the house last week and so  far the opposition says they won't  support it the ndp says it doesn't do  enough to help people still struggling  and the conservatives have a number of  demands including getting the finance  committee back up and running to study  it lots to work out with just a couple  more weeks until the holiday break  abigail beeman global news ottawa  in edmonton members of the metis nation  are preparing to meet pope francis at  the vatican later this month metis first  nations and inuit delegations will each  have an hour to speak privately with the  pontiff about the role of the catholic  church in residential schools  so to have that acknowledgement  is is a great  is a great gift to us  and we have our stories going there  and some of these stories are  cemented  they're  they're already  done  but there should be new stories coming  back  and that's what i'm hoping for are the  new stories  leaders and residential school survivors  from the metis nation will meet with  pope francis on december 18th the pope  is planning to visit canada but no date  has been set  omicron anxiety some advice before you  pack your bags  it's been a busy few days for canadian  travel agents the newly discovered  omicron variant and subsequent travel  bans and changing restrictions are  creating a lot of confusion this holiday  season and gaviola has more on what you  need to know about air travel and  insurance  before news of the omicron variant broke  canada's airline industry was set to hit  a pandemic era high this holiday season  it'll take time to see whether this  