ola  global news toronto  next the push to give canada's frontline  workers royal recognition  you're watching global national  when queen elizabeth marked 60 years on  the throne in 2012 the canadian  government seized the moment to honor  its own citizens the diamond jubilee  medal was created and has been awarded  to canadians from all walks of life for  their service to community and country  well as the queen approaches her 70th  year on the throne there are calls to  honor frontline workers who have given  so much in the pandemic but as david  aiken explains there are no plans for  more medals  during the 2012 jubilee special medals  were given to thousands of deserving  canadians rcmp members the military  volunteers indigenous leaders  prince charles himself toured the  country to hand some out as did then  prime minister stephen harper thank you  very much  olympic gold medalist adam vancouverdin  now an mp himself also received a  diamond jubilee medal for his  accomplishments in sport the athletes  were all brought up to uh the house of  commons to go on to the onto the carpet  and meet a whole bunch of mps and it was  a very special moment for a lot of us  but there may be no such special moments  for deserving canadians next year the  queen's platinum jubilee year  the royal canadian legion among others  has been pushing the trudeau government  for two years to commit to a medal  program but so far its requests have  been ignored are we going to lose  something by not having a diamond  jubilee medal  we'll live  but we'll live more poorly because of it  quebec mp pierre paulus even made a  direct appeal writing a letter to the  queen you know with the panamic we have  a lot of stories of people being  involved and with 12 canadians and i  don't understand why justin trudeau and  his government don't want that meadows  another mp cheryl gallant put a petition  before the house of commons with more  than 1800 signatures asking for a  jubilee medal program